# §7703. Determination of marital status

> Module Section7703

> Using SaraWorld as W
> Using SaraKinship as K
> Using SaraPredicates as P

Port of `section7703.pl`. §7703 decides whether an individual counts as married
for a taxable year: subsection (a) is the general rule, and subsection (b) takes
certain married individuals living apart *out* of that status.

## The §152 ⇄ §7703 cycle, stratified

§7703(b)(1) requires a child for whom the taxpayer gets a §151 deduction, which
routes through §152; §152 in turn asks §7703 whether someone is married. Catala
rejects cyclic definitions, so the port stratifies at the point where the cycle
is thinnest:

| level | computed from |
|---|---|
| 1. §7703(a) | events only — **no §152 dependency** |
| 2. §152 | using level 1 as its marital-status input |
| 3. §7703(b) | using level 2 as its dependency input |
| 4. §7703 | level 1 and not level 3 |

Level 1 is genuinely free of the cycle, which is what makes the stratification
honest rather than arbitrary: subsection (a) reads only marriage, death and
legal-separation events. The cut is recorded in `sara_port/README.md`.

## Helpers

```catala-metadata
## An event's amount list, named so the (b)(2) sums read cleanly.
declaration e_amounts content list of money
  depends on ev content W.Event
  equals ev.amounts
```

## (a)(1) Determination as of the close of the taxable year

A marriage counts if it began on or before the last day of the year — the Prolog
defaults a missing start to the first day of the year — and had not ended before
the year closed. If the spouse died during the year, the determination is made
as of the death instead.

```catala-metadata
## `is_before/2` compares with `=<`, so every window test here is inclusive.
declaration scope MarriageStatus:
  input world content W.World
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input spouse content W.Entity
  input marriage content W.Event
  input taxable_year content integer
  ## The marriage's candidate start dates. SARA writes the default as a
  ## *disjunction*, `( \+ start_(M,_), S = First_day_year ; start_(M,S) )`, so
  ## with several recorded starts it backtracks over every one of them and the
  ## clause holds if any satisfies the tests below. Reading one date here made
  ## the port answer false where SARA retries and succeeds (DEVIATIONS.md D74).
  output start_candidates content list of date
  ## The spouse's death, if it falls inside the taxable year.
  output spouse_died_on content optional of date
  output holds_a_1 content boolean
```

```catala
scope MarriageStatus:
  definition start_candidates equals
    if (number of marriage.starts) = 0
    then [W.first_day_year of taxable_year]
    else marriage.starts

  definition spouse_died_on equals
    List.first_element of
      (combine all ds
        among (map each ev among
                (list of e among world.events
                 such that e.kinds contains W.EventKind.Death
                           and e.agents contains spouse)
               to (list of d among ev.starts
                   such that (W.first_day_year of taxable_year) <= d
                             and d <= (W.last_day_year of taxable_year)))
        in acc initially []
        with acc ++ ds)

  definition holds_a_1 equals
    exists s among start_candidates such that
    s <= (W.last_day_year of taxable_year)
    and (match spouse_died_on with pattern
         -- Present content death:
             # determination made as of the time of death
             s <= death
             and ((number of marriage.ends) = 0
                  or (exists e among marriage.ends such that death <= e))
         -- Absent:
             # otherwise the marriage must run into the next year
             (if (number of marriage.ends) = 0
              then
                # No end date: the spouse's death is what ends the marriage, so
                # it must fall on or after 1 January next year for the marriage
                # to still be running at the close of the year.
                #
                # The test is on the death *event*, not on the death *dates*.
                # SARA writes
                #
                #     ( death_(D), agent_(D,Spouse) )
                #     ->  ( start_(D,End_time), is_before(First_day_next,End_time) )
                #     ;   true
                #
                # so a death event carrying no date does not fall through to
                # `true`: `start_/2` fails and the whole of (a)(1) fails with
                # it. Collecting the dates first and asking whether the list is
                # empty answers a different question, and made the port call a
                # taxpayer married whose spouse had an undated death.
                #
                # `->` also commits to the first solution of its condition, so
                # only the *first* such death event is consulted; a later dated
                # one cannot rescue an earlier undated one.
                (match (List.first_element of
                          (list of e among world.events
                           such that e.kinds contains W.EventKind.Death
                                     and e.agents contains spouse)) with pattern
                 -- Absent: true
                 -- Present content dv:
                     exists d among dv.starts such that
                       (W.first_day_year of (taxable_year + 1)) <= d)
              else
                exists e among marriage.ends such that
                  (W.first_day_year of (taxable_year + 1)) <= e))
```

## (a)(2) Legal separation

A decree of divorce or of separate maintenance, entered on or before the last
day of the year, whose patient is the marriage. The decree kind sits in the
*agent* role, which is why `SaraWorld.EntityTag` carries it.

```catala-metadata
declaration scope LegalSeparation:
  input world content W.World
  input marriage content W.Event
  input taxable_year content integer
  output separated content boolean
```

```catala
scope LegalSeparation:
  definition separated equals
    exists ev among world.events such that
      ev.kinds contains W.EventKind.LegalSeparation
      and (ev.patients contains marriage.ident)
      and (exists a among ev.agents such that
             a.tag = W.EntityTag.DecreeOfDivorce
             or a.tag = W.EntityTag.DecreeOfSeparateMaintenance)
      and (exists d among ev.starts such that
             d <= (W.last_day_year of taxable_year))
```

## (a) General rule

`s7703_a` holds for a taxpayer when some marriage satisfies (a)(1) and is not
undone by (a)(2). The cases query it existentially — `s7703_a_1(alice,_,_,_,2012)`
leaves both the spouse and the marriage unbound — so the scope reports whether
any candidate qualifies, and which spouse.

```catala-metadata
declaration structure Candidate:
  data spouse content W.Entity
  data marriage content W.Event

declaration scope MaritalStatusA:
  input world content W.World
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  ## Every (spouse, marriage) the taxpayer appears in.
  output candidates content list of Candidate
  ## s7703_a_1/5 — some candidate satisfies (a)(1)
  output holds_a_1 content boolean
  ## s7703_a_2/5 — some candidate marriage is legally separated
  output holds_a_2 content boolean
  ## s7703_a/4
  output married content boolean
  ## Every spouse the taxpayer is married to under (a). `s7703_a/4` is a
  ## generator, and §151(b) asks about a *named* spouse, so the whole set is
  ## reported rather than only the first.
  output spouses content list of W.Entity
  output spouse content optional of W.Entity
```

```catala
scope MaritalStatusA:
  definition candidates equals
    combine all cs
      among (map each ev among
              (list of e among world.events
               such that e.kinds contains W.EventKind.Marriage
                         and e.agents contains taxpayer)
             to (map each sp among
                   (list of a among ev.agents such that a.id != taxpayer.id)
                 to Candidate { -- spouse: sp -- marriage: ev }))
      in acc initially []
      with acc ++ cs

  definition holds_a_1 equals
    exists c among candidates such that
      (output of MarriageStatus with {
         -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer -- spouse: c.spouse
         -- marriage: c.marriage -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).holds_a_1

  definition holds_a_2 equals
    exists c among candidates such that
      (output of LegalSeparation with {
         -- world: world -- marriage: c.marriage
         -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).separated

  definition married equals
    exists c among candidates such that
      (output of MarriageStatus with {
         -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer -- spouse: c.spouse
         -- marriage: c.marriage -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).holds_a_1
      and not (output of LegalSeparation with {
         -- world: world -- marriage: c.marriage
         -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).separated

  definition spouses equals
    map each c among
      (list of c among candidates such that
        (output of MarriageStatus with {
           -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer -- spouse: c.spouse
           -- marriage: c.marriage -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).holds_a_1
        and not (output of LegalSeparation with {
           -- world: world -- marriage: c.marriage
           -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).separated)
     to c.spouse

  definition spouse equals List.first_element of spouses
```

## (b) Certain married individuals living apart

All three paragraphs must hold. (b)(1) reaches §152, which is why this is
level 3 of the stratification: the §152 verdict arrives as an input.

### (b)(1) Maintains a home for a qualifying child for more than half the year

```catala-metadata
declaration scope LivingApartOne:
  input world content W.World
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input household content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  ## §152(a)(1) for some dependant residing in this household -- supplied by
  ## the caller at level 2 of the stratification.
  input qualifying_dependants content list of W.Entity
  output holds content boolean
```

```catala
scope LivingApartOne:
  definition holds equals
    # files a separate return
    (not (exists ev among world.events such that
            ev.kinds contains W.EventKind.JointReturn
            and ev.agents contains taxpayer
            and ev.starts contains (W.first_day_year of taxable_year)
            and ev.ends contains (W.last_day_year of taxable_year)))
    # maintains as his home the household
    and (exists rt among world.events such that
           rt.kinds contains W.EventKind.Residence
           and rt.agents contains taxpayer
           and rt.patients contains household)
    # which is the child's principal place of abode for more than half the year
    and (exists dep among qualifying_dependants such that
           (exists rc among
             (list of e among world.events
              such that e.kinds contains W.EventKind.Residence
                        and e.agents contains dep
                        and e.patients contains household)
            such that
              (exists st among rc.starts such that
                 (let span_start equals
                    (if st >= (W.first_day_year of taxable_year)
                     then st else (W.first_day_year of taxable_year)) in
                  let span_end equals
                    (match (K.earliest of
                             ((K.opt_dates of rc.ends)
                              ++ [Present content (W.last_day_year of taxable_year)]))
                     with pattern
                     -- Absent: W.last_day_year of taxable_year
                     -- Present content d: d) in
                  (span_end - span_start) * 2
                    >= ((W.last_day_year of taxable_year)
                        - (W.first_day_year of taxable_year))))))
```

### (b)(2) Furnishes over half the cost of maintaining the household

The two `findall`s differ in exactly one literal — the taxpayer's payments are
those with `agent_(Payment,Taxp)`, the denominator drops that condition. A
payment counts when its purpose names either the residence event or the
household itself, and when its start date falls in the taxable year (the Prolog
compares only the year part of the date string).

```catala-metadata
declaration payment_for_household content boolean
  depends on ev content W.Event, world content W.World,
             household content W.Entity, y content integer
  equals
    ev.kinds contains W.EventKind.Payment
    and (ev.purposes contains (W.Purpose.PurposeEntity content household)
         or (exists r among
              (list of e among world.events
               such that e.kinds contains W.EventKind.Residence
                         and e.patients contains household)
             such that ev.purposes contains
                         (W.Purpose.PurposeEntity content r.ident)))
    and (exists d among ev.starts such that Date.get_year of d = y)

declaration scope LivingApartTwo:
  input world content W.World
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input household content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  output cost content money
  output furnished content money
  output holds content boolean
```

```catala
scope LivingApartTwo:
  definition cost equals
    Money.sum of
      (map each ev among
        (list of e among world.events
         such that payment_for_household of e, world, household, taxable_year)
       to Money.sum of e_amounts of ev)

  definition furnished equals
    Money.sum of
      (map each ev among
        (list of e among world.events
         such that (payment_for_household of e, world, household, taxable_year)
                   and e.agents contains taxpayer)
       to Money.sum of e_amounts of ev)

  definition holds equals cost > $0 and (furnished * (decimal of 2)) >= cost
```

### (b)(3) The spouse is not a member of the household in the last six months

The Prolog enumerates day offsets 2 through 185 from 1 July — which SWI
normalises through to 1 January of the next year — tests membership on each, and
requires zero hits:

```prolog
between(2,185,Day_offset),
date_time_stamp(date(Taxy,7,Day_offset,0,0,0,0,-,-), Stamp),
... s7703_b_3_is_member_of_household(Spouse,Household,Day)
```

Membership on a day `D` means `start =< D` and, if the residence has an end,
`D =< end`. So membership on *some* day of the window is exactly the residence
interval meeting `[2 July, 1 January]`, and the day-by-day scan reduces to an
interval intersection: `start =< 1 January` and, where there is an end,
`end >= 2 July`. The port tests that closed form rather than enumerating 184
days, which is the same predicate and does not need duration arithmetic Catala
reserves for literals.

```catala-metadata
declaration scope LivingApartThree:
  input world content W.World
  input spouse content W.Entity
  input household content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  output window_start content date
  output window_end content date
  output any_membership content boolean
  output holds content boolean
```

```catala
scope LivingApartThree:
  definition window_start equals Date.of_year_month_day of taxable_year, 7, 2
  definition window_end equals Date.of_year_month_day of (taxable_year + 1), 1, 1

  definition any_membership equals
    exists ev among world.events such that
      ev.kinds contains W.EventKind.Residence
      and ev.agents contains spouse
      and ev.patients contains household
      and (exists st among ev.starts such that st <= window_end)
      and ((number of ev.ends) = 0
           or (exists en among ev.ends such that en >= window_start))

  definition holds equals not any_membership
```

## (b) as a whole, and §7703 itself

`s7703_b(Taxp,Spouse,Taxy)` requires all three paragraphs *of the same
household*, and `s7703/4` is subsection (a) minus that. The household is
generated from the taxpayer's own residence events, which is where the Prolog's
`residence_(Taxp_residence), patient_(Taxp_residence,Household)` puts it.

This is level 3–4 of the stratification at the top of this file: §152 arrives
as `qualifying_dependants` rather than being computed here, so the module stays
free of the cycle. `Section151` is the first caller that supplies it for real.

```catala-metadata
## `list_to_set` over the two sources of a spouse.
declaration dedup_spouses content list of W.Entity
  depends on l content list of W.Entity
  equals
    combine all x among l in acc initially []
    with (if (exists a among acc such that a.id = x.id) then acc else acc ++ [x])

declaration scope MaritalStatus:
  input world content W.World
  ## A case may *grant* `s7703/4` rather than model the marriage, and one that
  ## grants it without declaring the predicate discontiguous has replaced the
  ## whole of §7703: the derivation is gone and only the rows answer. See D65.
  input injections content list of W.Injection
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  ## §152(a)(1) dependants, from level 2.
  input qualifying_dependants content list of W.Entity
  ## Every household the taxpayer resides at.
  output households content list of W.Entity
  ## The (a) spouses that (b) does *not* take back out.
  output derived_spouses content list of W.Entity
  ## ... and the ones a case named outright.
  output granted_spouses content list of W.Entity
  output spouses content list of W.Entity
  output spouse content optional of W.Entity
  ## s7703_b/3 — true when (a) held but (b) removed every spouse.
  output living_apart content boolean
  ## s7703/4
  output married content boolean
```

```catala
scope MaritalStatus:
  definition households equals
    combine all ps
      among (map each ev among
              (list of e among world.events
               such that e.kinds contains W.EventKind.Residence
                         and e.agents contains taxpayer)
             to ev.patients)
      in acc initially []
      with acc ++ ps

  definition derived_spouses equals
    list of sp among
      (output of MaritalStatusA with {
         -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer
         -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).spouses
    such that
      not (exists h among households such that
             (output of LivingApartOne with {
                -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer -- household: h
                -- taxable_year: taxable_year
                -- qualifying_dependants: qualifying_dependants }).holds
             and (output of LivingApartTwo with {
                    -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer -- household: h
                    -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).holds
             and (output of LivingApartThree with {
                    -- world: world -- spouse: sp -- household: h
                    -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).holds)

  definition granted_spouses equals
    list of e among
      (map each inj among
        (W.injections_for of injections, P.pred_s7703_4,
           [taxpayer.id; -1; -1; W.num_key of taxable_year])
       to (match (W.injection_entity of inj, 2) with pattern
           -- Absent: taxpayer
           -- Present content sp: sp))
    such that e.id != taxpayer.id

  definition spouses equals
    dedup_spouses of
      ((if W.pred_overridden of injections, P.pred_s7703_4
        then [] else derived_spouses)
       ++ granted_spouses)

  definition spouse equals List.first_element of spouses

  definition married equals (number of spouses) > 0

  definition living_apart equals
    (output of MaritalStatusA with {
       -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer
       -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).married
    and (number of derived_spouses) = 0
```

## The spouse a joint return was filed with

`gross_income/3` in `utils.pl` adds the spouse's income to the taxpayer's when
the two filed a joint return covering the whole taxable year, and §63, §68 and
§151(d)(3) all read gross income through it. The spouse has to survive the
whole of §7703, so the test belongs here.

```catala-metadata
declaration scope JointFilingSpouse:
  input world content W.World
  input injections content list of W.Injection
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  ## §152(a)(1) dependants, for (b)(1) — as `MaritalStatus` takes them.
  input qualifying_dependants content list of W.Entity
  output spouse content optional of W.Entity
```

```catala
scope JointFilingSpouse:
  definition spouse equals
    List.first_element of
      (list of sp among
        (output of MaritalStatus with {
           -- world: world -- injections: injections -- taxpayer: taxpayer
           -- taxable_year: taxable_year
           -- qualifying_dependants: qualifying_dependants }).spouses
       such that
         exists jr among world.events such that
           jr.kinds contains W.EventKind.JointReturn
           and jr.agents contains taxpayer
           and jr.agents contains sp
           and jr.starts contains (W.first_day_year of taxable_year)
           and jr.ends contains (W.last_day_year of taxable_year))
```
